Reading it: if the rate climbs with partner count among polar tips,
the rule is failing exactly where a hydrogen bond determines the
answer, and the missing ingredient is a feature rather than capacity.
If it is flat or falls, the hydrogen-bonding story is wrong and SER
is simply small and under-determined -- in which case compare
against what the baselines score on SER before calling it ours.
The non-polar row is the control: a CG carbon cannot hydrogen bond,
so any trend there is crowding, not chemistry.

